//! task: write
//! ask: Build an array of four u32 values from a literal and sum it with a loop.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.6
//! explain: `[e1, …, en]` is an array literal of type `acies<T, n>`; `N` is part of the type. `[e; N]` repeats one value N times (the way to ask for zeros, since nothing is zero-filled). In `per i in 0..4`, a range of two literals types as `mensura`, which is what indexes an array.

publica functio summa() -> u32 {
    firma v: acies<u32, 4> = [1, 2, 3, 4];
    mutabilis s: u32 = 0;
    per i in 0..4 {
        s = s + v[i];
    }
    redde s;
}
